From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000016 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] sunxi: cubie-a7s: do not start the ARISC

CMD_SUNXI_BOOT_ARISC defaults to y on the A733, and pxe_utils runs it
before each extlinux boot (3af827d845). It copies the trained DRAM
parameters out of the DRAM blob in SRAM into the kernel's device tree
(603e7ff4b9) and asks BL31 to start the E902 with SMC 0x8000ff10
(1210558a46, 238d06aac9). This chain loads no SCP image, and its BL31,
built from TF-A source, answers that call with SMC_UNK. Turn the command
off, so the kernel gets its device tree unchanged and no call is made.

Assisted-by: Claude
---
diff --git a/configs/radxa-cubie-a7s_defconfig b/configs/radxa-cubie-a7s_defconfig
index 8d089424099..fe4cbaa300f 100644
--- a/configs/radxa-cubie-a7s_defconfig
+++ b/configs/radxa-cubie-a7s_defconfig
@@ -70,3 +70,4 @@ CONFIG_SYSRESET_PSCI=y
 CONFIG_DM_RNG=y
 CONFIG_RNG_SUN60I_CE=y
 CONFIG_CMD_RNG=y
+# CONFIG_CMD_SUNXI_BOOT_ARISC is not set
